hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1334","Ubayd Allah ibn al-Jahm al-Anmati narrated to us, Ayoub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah al-Shaybani, Yahya ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, Ibn al-Dailami narrated to us On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, and Ibrahim bin Munqidh bin Abdullah Al-Khawlani narrated to us, Ayoub, meaning Ibn Suwayd, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, and he is Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Shaibani, on the authority of Abu Busr Abdullah bin Al-Dili, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When Suleiman bin Dawud finished building the Holy Mosque, he asked God for a ruling that coincided with his ruling. And a kingdom that no one after him should have, and no one will come to this mosque who only wants to pray in it, unless he is free from his sin like the day his mother gave birth to him.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for two, I have given them, and I hope that I have given the third.”"
